    "about.title": "About",
    "about.subtitle": "kcore is built by Tacconi Consulting Ltd, a platform engineering consultancy based in England.",
    "about.company": "Tacconi Consulting Ltd",
    "about.desc1": "We help teams design, build, and operate reliable platforms, and accelerate software delivery with spec-driven code generation and pragmatic AI workflows.",
    "about.desc2": "kcore grew out of our infrastructure work. We kept running into the same problem: managing VMs on bare metal was either too manual or required buying into a heavyweight platform. So we built something that fits how we actually work &mdash; declarative, API-driven, and simple enough to run on a single node or scale across many.",
    "about.openCoreTitle": "Open core and licensing",
    "about.openCoreLead": "kcore uses an open-core model: the platform core is Apache-2.0, and subscriptions cover the official supported distribution, curated production updates, and commercial support. Pricing is per physical CPU socket; details are on the pricing page.",
    "about.openCoreLink": "Pricing and editions",
    "about.infra.title": "Infrastructure",
    "about.infra.desc": "Kubernetes (including bare metal), GitOps with Argo CD, platform engineering, and day-2 operations. Deterministic upgrades, runbooks, and operational clarity. Linux, virtualisation, AWS where it fits.",
    "about.ai.title": "AI Engineering",
    "about.ai.desc": "Spec-driven code generation &mdash; scaffolding, clients, tests, and contracts with human review and CI gates. Structured support for legacy modernisation and pragmatic AI adoption.",
    "about.who": "Who we work with",
    "about.who1": "Organisations looking for pragmatic AI adoption &mdash; without hype.",
    "about.who2": "Teams modernising legacy estates with a structured approach.",
    "about.who3": "Regulated or on-prem environments where control and auditability matter.",
    "about.who4": "Platform and infrastructure teams that need reliability and clear ownership.",
    "about.how": "How we work",
    "about.how.desc": "Same discipline across infrastructure and software: discovery, architecture, implementation, handover. For AI-assisted work: human-in-the-loop, tests first, CI gates before merge. Automation and CI from the start; documentation and runbooks as deliverables.",
