    "userdoc.firstcluster.li.next1": "<a href=\"add-node.html\">Add more nodes</a> — agent-only nodes, HA controllers, cross-DC.",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.li.next2": "<a href=\"images.html\">Upload images</a> — for air-gapped or large image files.",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.li.next3": "<a href=\"networks.html\">Create networks</a> — NAT, bridge, or VXLAN overlay.",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.note.approve": "Pending nodes cannot schedule workloads. Approval is a human gate on top of mTLS.",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.p.approve": "After boot the node agent registers with its local controller and appears as <strong>pending</strong>:",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.p.boot": "Boot the server from the kcore ISO. The live environment starts a node-agent listening on <code>:9091</code>.",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.p.createvm": "See <a href=\"vm-creation.html\">VM creation</a> for all options including YAML manifests, SSH keys, and cloud-init.",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.p.discover": "Identify the OS disk (e.g. <code>/dev/sda</code>) and any data disks.",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.p.install1": "Use <code>--run-controller</code> to start a controller on this node. The OS disk is partitioned with LUKS encryption (TPM2-sealed when available).",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.p.install2": "The node reboots into the installed NixOS system. The controller listens on <code>:9090</code> and the node agent on <code>:9091</code>.",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.p.intro": "This walkthrough creates a single-node kcore cluster: one machine running both the controller and the node agent, ready to schedule VMs.",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.p.pki1": "On your operator workstation (where <code>kctl</code> is installed):",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.p.pki2": "This generates the root CA, sub-CA, controller certificate, and <code>kctl</code> client certificate under <code>~/.kcore/prod/</code>.",
    "userdoc.firstcluster.p.verify": "The node should show status <strong>ready</strong> and approval <strong>approved</strong>.",
