    "blog.post7.title": "Security groups: nginx NAT network (before and after)",
    "blog.post7.date": "11 April 2026",
    "blog.post7.summary": "RFC1918 lab addresses, curl before after, security group manifest DNAT host TCP/8080 overlay guest nginx।",
    "bp.sg.title": "Security groups: nginx NAT network (before and after)",
    "bp.sg.date": "11 April 2026",
    "bp.sg.back": "← ब्लॉग पर वापस",
    "bp.sg.intro1": "NAT-backed overlay workload private address listen physical host expose nothing until security group opens (optionally DNATs) traffic। host LAN IP curl nginx hit नहीं until policy।",
    "bp.sg.intro2": "commands realistic RFC1918 lab: host <code>192.168.40.105</code>, overlay guest <code>10.250.0.7</code>, node id <code>kvm-node-192-168-40-105</code>, network <code>private</code>। own names IPs substitute।",
    "bp.sg.note1": "<strong>Why VM manifest:</strong> Security group DNAT <code>targetVm</code> resolves <strong>VM workload's</strong> stored private IP controller today। nginx OCI container same NAT same forwarding; VM-shaped flow below copy-paste <code>kctl describe vm</code> <code>targetVm</code> match।",
    "bp.sg.h2prereq": "Prerequisites",
    "bp.sg.prereq1": "Controller operator machine reachable; <code>kctl</code> configured।",
    "bp.sg.prereq2": "NAT-style network named <code>private</code> (manifest change) node attached।",
    "bp.sg.prereq3": "Debian or similar image VM creation registered (other quickstarts)।",
    "bp.sg.h2step1": "1) Run nginx overlay",
    "bp.sg.step1desc": "Small VM workload nginx port 80 guest। controller overlay address <code>10.250.0.7</code> network <code>private</code>।",
    "bp.sg.step1b": "guest nginx install start (cloud-init or SSH) <code>0.0.0.0:80</code> listen। private IP confirm:",
    "bp.sg.step1c": "line table entry <code>10.250.0.7</code> (overlay range another address) expect।",
    "bp.sg.h2step2": "2) From host curl fails without security group",
    "bp.sg.step2desc": "hypervisor host (<code>192.168.40.105</code>) overlay address ingress/DNAT not wired:",
    "bp.sg.step2out": "first request timeout refuse; second host address nothing port 8080 published yet।",
    "bp.sg.h2step3": "3) Declare security group (DNAT host 8080 → guest 80)",
    "bp.sg.step3desc": "following <code>expose-nginx.yaml</code> save। network node attach TCP host external IP port 8080 guest private IP port 80।",
    "bp.sg.h2step4": "4) Apply and reconcile",
    "bp.sg.step4desc": "node reconcile Nix nftables wait (usually one controller/node sync cycle)। NAT network different external IP <code>192.168.40.105</code> DNAT rule network <code>externalIP</code> node rendered keys off।",
    "bp.sg.h2step5": "5) Curl succeeds via host",
    "bp.sg.step5desc": "any machine node LAN reach:",
    "bp.sg.step5b": "HTTP 200 nginx response headers expect। traffic DNATted 10.250.0.7:80 overlay inside।",
    "bp.sg.h2container": "nginx container?",
    "bp.sg.container1": "<code>kctl workload create --kind container nginx-demo ... --network private</code> create one। isolation same: service private address host Ethernet port until policy path opens।",
    "bp.sg.container2": "DNAT container endpoints controller bind directly until container VM front pair or VM flow above <code>targetVm</code> rules। product repo <a href=\"https://github.com/kcorehypervisor/kcore/blob/main/docs/security-groups.md\" style=\"color: var(--accent-primary);\">security-groups.md</a> rule model।",
    "bp.sg.outro": "more examples kcore tree <a href=\"https://github.com/kcorehypervisor/kcore/blob/main/examples/security-groups/expose-nginx-host.yaml\" style=\"color: var(--accent-primary);\">expose-nginx-host.yaml</a>।",
